# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# backend/.env.production.example — SERVER-SIDE DELTA, not a full config file
#
# This file lists ONLY the keys whose value MUST DIFFER on an always-on Linux
# host from the Windows development machine, plus the secrets that must be
# copied across. Every other key in backend/.env.example is environment-
# independent: copy it over unchanged.
#
# TARGETS — the same image and the same compose file serve all three. Where a
# key's value differs BETWEEN targets it is tagged inline:
#
#   [A] Raspberry Pi 400   arm64, 4 GB, home LAN behind NAT, no public IP
#   [B] Oracle Cloud A1    arm64, 12 GB, Ubuntu, PUBLIC IP
#   [C] x86_64 VPS         (Hetzner et al.) — behaves like [B] in every respect
#
# Untagged keys are identical on every target.
#
# Deployment recipe:
#   1. scp backend/.env  ->  server:<repo>/backend/.env
#   2. apply every override in this file to that copy
#   3. docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d --build
#
# NOT IN THIS FILE — container/network knobs live in the ROOT .env, because they
# configure Docker rather than the application:
#   API_BIND_HOST   the host interface the API is published on. Default
#                   127.0.0.1 (loopback, correct for [B]/[C]); 0.0.0.0 is the
#                   LAN-browsable choice for [A] and is acceptable ONLY behind
#                   NAT with no port-forward. The app itself always listens on
#                   0.0.0.0 inside its container — that is not configurable and
#                   does not need to be.
#   API_PORT, *_MEM_LIMIT, *_CPUS, PG_*   see .env.example at the repo root.
# Full per-target matrix: DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# All values below are intentionally EMPTY (repo rule: no secrets, no defaults).
# The comment above each key states what to put there and why it must change.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. MUST CHANGE — Windows paths do not exist on Linux ─────────────────────
#
# VAULT_PATH on the dev machine is `C:/SecondBrain`, an Obsidian vault that does
# not and will not exist on the server. On Linux that string is not an absolute
# path at all — it is parsed as a RELATIVE directory literally named "C:", which
# Path.mkdir(parents=True) will happily CREATE inside the container. Nothing
# errors. The weekly Sunday chain then writes a journal into that junk directory,
# ships it to the Anthropic API, and BURNS CREDITS summarising an empty week into
# a vault nobody will ever read.
#
# Two independent defences, set BOTH:
#   * WIKI_INGEST_ENABLED=false  — scheduler skips the whole weekly chain
#     (journal → ingest → promote). This is the one that stops the spend.
#   * VAULT_PATH=/app/vault      — a real absolute Linux path, backed by the
#     `vault` named volume in docker-compose.prod.yml, so if the chain is ever
#     enabled server-side it writes somewhere legitimate.
#
VAULT_PATH=
WIKI_INGEST_ENABLED=


# ── 2. MUST CHANGE — the database lives on the compose network ───────────────
#
# Dev value points at localhost (the Docker-published Postgres port). Inside
# compose the database is the service named `db` and port 5432 is NOT published
# to the host at all.
#
#   dev :  postgresql://trader:trader@localhost:5432/trading
#   prod:  postgresql://trader:trader@db:5432/trading
#
# NOTE: docker-compose.prod.yml ALREADY sets this via its `environment:` block,
# which takes precedence over env_file. Setting it here too is belt-and-braces
# for anyone running the container outside compose.
DATABASE_URL=


# ── 3. MUST CHANGE — CORS ─────────────────────────────────── [A] differs ────
#
# Dev value is the Vite dev server (http://localhost:5173). No frontend ships
# with docker-compose.prod.yml, so this only matters for browser JS, never for
# curl or for opening a URL directly.
#
#   [B]/[C] loopback + SSH tunnel: the origin you actually browse from is
#           http://localhost:8000 (or http://localhost:<local tunnel port>).
#           Set exactly that, or leave it as the dev value — harmless.
#
#   [A] Pi on the LAN: if you later serve the React app from another machine and
#       point it at the Pi, the BROWSER's origin must be listed here or every
#       fetch fails CORS. Comma-separated, no spaces, scheme + host + port, e.g.
#           http://tradeai.local:5173,http://192.168.1.50:5173
#       Opening http://tradeai.local:8000/api/v1/shadow/performance directly in a
#       browser is NOT a cross-origin request and needs nothing here.
#
# Do NOT set `*` — app/main.py passes allow_credentials=True, and the wildcard is
# rejected by browsers in that combination anyway.
CORS_ORIGINS=


# ── 4. MUST COPY — secrets (never committed, never baked into an image) ──────
#
# These have no dev/prod distinction in VALUE, but the server has no copy of them
# until you put one there. Missing OANDA keys = no candles, no pricing, no
# signals. Missing FRED key = macro series go stale and six of the nineteen model
# features silently NaN on every live signal (the exact failure the macro
# staleness watchdog was added for).
#
# OANDA — also re-confirm the URLs are the PRACTICE endpoints. Practice vs live
# is URL-only in this platform; deploying with the live URLs is the entire
# difference between observing and trading real money.
OANDA_API_KEY=
OANDA_ACCOUNT_ID=
OANDA_BASE_URL=
OANDA_STREAM_URL=

# FRED — macro_data pipeline (fundamentals cron A/B)
FUNDAMENTAL_DATA_API_KEY=

# Anthropic — only needed if WIKI_INGEST_ENABLED is ever set true on the server.
# Leave EMPTY while the wiki chain is disabled; an absent key is a second
# independent guarantee that no credits can be spent from this host.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# ── 5. VERIFY BEFORE EVERY DEPLOY — the safety flags ────────────────────────
#
# M8-Shadow is an OBSERVE-ONLY deployment. These three lines are what make that
# true by construction; re-read them on every deploy rather than assuming.
#
#   ORDER_PLACEMENT_ENABLED=false
#       Hard flag. BrokerClient.place_order refuses every order while false, and
#       BrokerRouter re-checks before routing. Never set true while ML_MODEL_PATH
#       points at a `.NOT_PROMOTED` artifact — inference refuses that combination
#       at load time, so the container would fail to start (correctly).
#
#   SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED=true
#       The reason this deployment exists. With it true, the app now FAILS TO
#       START if the artifact at ML_MODEL_PATH cannot be loaded — no more silent
#       zero-row deployments.
#
#   ML_MODEL_PATH
#       Relative paths resolve against backend/. The artifact lives in
#       backend/models/, which is GITIGNORED — it is NOT in a fresh clone.
#       You must copy it to the server manually:
#           scp backend/models/* server:<repo>/backend/models/
#       .dockerignore deliberately does NOT exclude models/, so it is baked into
#       the image at build time.
ORDER_PLACEMENT_ENABLED=
SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED=
ML_MODEL_PATH=
ML_ALLOW_UNPROMOTED_MODEL=


# ── 6. CONSIDER CHANGING — alert delivery ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Dev uses `log`, which is fine when someone is watching a terminal. On an
# unattended server the price-stream outage escalation and the circuit breaker
# have nobody to tell. `telegram` or `email` makes those alerts reach you.
# (Both are scaffolds in app/services/alerts/ — implement before relying on them.)
ALERT_DELIVERY=


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOT changed on the server (listed so nobody "fixes" them):
#
#   RISK_* / ATR_* / MIN_RR_RATIO / SIGNAL_*   — the strategy is the strategy;
#       identical values are what make dev results and server results comparable.
#   ML_* training hyperparameters              — reproducibility identity of the
#       artifact (params_hash). Changing them invalidates the model card.
#   EXECUTION_WINDOW_* / MID_WARMUP_START      — properties of the CORPUS, not of
#       the host.
#   BACKTEST_*                                 — the promotion gate is a fixed
#       standard, not an environment setting.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
